hume-dialogues-1.md:1: argue/answered: S4: answered no, which keeps hume-dialogues-1.logic.r1.2 and hume-dialogues-1.logic.r1.3, to: Suppose "the one has no more weight than the other" is true and "the mind remains in suspense between them" and "scepticism triumphs" are false. Is S4, "The mind must remain in suspense between them; and it is that very suspense or balance, which is the triumph of scepticism.", true then?
